                                Virgin and Jesus)</orgName>
                            <p><q>Memorandum quod Maister <persName role="dnr" key="person_3985"
                                        >Galfridus Downes</persName> vult quod liber iste post
                                    mortem Maistri(?) <persName>Jacobi Downes</persName> donetur
                                    capelle de Potte etc in commitatu Schropschyrre.</q> G. Downes,
                                Fellow of Queens' College Cambridge (1490-4), by will dated 7 June
                                1492 founded the chapel of Pott Shrigley. <bibl>See Earwacker,
                                        <title>East Cheshire</title>, ii (1880), pp. 325-332.</bibl>
                                Note that more recent research casts doubt on whether the book
                                arrived; see <bibl>James Willoughby, <title>The Libraries of
                                        Collegiate Churches</title> (London, 2013), p.
                                406.</bibl></p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">Fol. 2: <q>Orate pro anima domini
                                    <persName>Hugonis Blyth</persName></q> (? Hugh B. Rector of
                            Roding Abbess, d. 1455).</provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">Fol. 1: <q>Pray for the soule of
                                Maister John Crowland <note type="editorial">[d. 1493]</note>
                                ffelowe of the Quenes College of Cambrigge and parson of South
                                Wokyngton <note type="editorial">[Ockendon]</note> in Essex, Gyver
                                of this boke."</q></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">Given by <persName>Lord
                                Dillon</persName> in 1924.</provenance>
